+# Pre-ship review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Reviewed: `packages/nextjs` frontend + config, against the deployed `Payouts` contract
+(`0x7c3f...b6F2`, Base 8453) and Base USDC (`0x8335...2913`).
+
+`yarn tsc --noEmit` passes — every issue below is behavioural, not a compile error.
+
+Scope note: report only, no code changed.
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. Disconnected users get a sentence, not a Connect button
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`**
+
+```tsx
+{!isConnected ? (
+  <p className="mt-4">Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p>
+```
+
+The whole page body is gated behind this, and the only way to connect is the header
+button. The primary action slot must *be* the connect action.
+
+**Fix:** render the scaffold button in the action slot:
+
+```tsx
+import { RainbowKitCustomConnectButton } from "~~/components/scaffold-eth";
+// ...
+if (!isConnected) return <RainbowKitCustomConnectButton />;
+```
+
+### 2. No wrong-network branch on the CTA — users sign on the wrong chain
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`**
+
+`targetNetworks` is `[base]` only, but nothing on the page checks `chain.id`. A wallet
+on Ethereum/Arbitrum sees fully live **Approve** and **Send Payout** buttons. `pay` will
+be sent to `0x7c3f...b6F2` on a chain where that address is not the Payouts contract —
+at best it reverts, at worst (an unrelated contract at that address) it does something
+unintended. The header's `WrongNetworkDropdown` does not stop the click.
+
+**Fix:** branch the action slot before Approve/Pay:
+
+```tsx
+const { chain } = useAccount();
+const { targetNetwork } = useTargetNetwork();
+const { switchChain } = useSwitchChain();
+
+if (chain?.id !== targetNetwork.id) {
+  return (
+    <button className="btn btn-primary" onClick={() => switchChain({ chainId: targetNetwork.id })}>
+      Switch to {targetNetwork.name}
+    </button>
+  );
+}
+```
+
+### 3. Writes bypass the scaffold hook
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:6,21,38,51`**
+
+```tsx
+import { useAccount, useWriteContract } from "wagmi";
+const { writeContractAsync, isPending } = useWriteContract();
+```
+
+Raw wagmi resolves at the **wallet signature**, not at confirmation. So `handlePay`
+clears the form (`:57-58`) the instant the user signs, before the tx is mined —
+the user sees an empty form and no idea whether the payout landed. It also skips
+scaffold's pre-flight simulation, the tx-progress notification and the explorer link.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```tsx
+const { writeContractAsync: writePayouts, isMining: isPaying } = useScaffoldWriteContract({
+  contractName: "Payouts",
+});
+await writePayouts({ functionName: "pay", args: [recipient, parseUnits(amount, 6), memo] });
+```
+
+Same for USDC `approve` (`contractName: "USDC"`, after issue 6 is fixed). Address and ABI
+then come from the registry instead of being hand-wired at `:39-42` / `:52-53`.
+
+### 4. Buttons unlock mid-flight → duplicate payouts
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101-110`**
+
+`isPending` drops as soon as the wallet returns the tx hash, ~1–2s before the tx is
+mined on Base. Both buttons re-enable while the payout is still in the mempool. On a
+30s polling interval (issue 12) the balance and feed still show the old state, so a
+user who doesn't see their payout appear will click **Send Payout** again and pay twice.
+Real money, no undo.
+
+**Fix:** gate on `isMining` from `useScaffoldWriteContract` (issue 3) — it is held across
+`waitForTransactionReceipt` and cleared in the hook's `finally` on both confirmation and
+rejection. If the balance/allowance refetch needs an extra hold after confirmation, keep
+it in local state and clear it in `finally`, never on a timer.
+
+### 5. Failed and rejected transactions fail silently
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46,59-61`**
+
+```tsx
+} catch (e) {
+  console.error(e);
+}
+```
+
+Insufficient allowance, insufficient USDC, user rejection, RPC error — all identical to
+the user: nothing happens. Nobody opens the console.
+
+**Fix:** surface it next to the action.
+
+```tsx
+import { getParsedError, notification } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";
+// ...
+} catch (e) {
+  notification.error(getParsedError(e));
+}
+```
+
+(Adopting `useScaffoldWriteContract` per issue 3 gives you most of this for free; keep an
+explicit catch for anything you want rendered inline.)
+
+### 6. USDC is hand-added to `deployedContracts.ts` — the next deploy deletes it
+**`packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50-134`** (and the file header at `:1-4`
+saying not to edit it)
+
+`deployedContracts.ts` is regenerated by `yarn deploy`. The next contract deploy wipes the
+`USDC` entry; `useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC" })` then silently returns
+nothing (balance renders `0`), `page.tsx:11` stops compiling, and approve breaks. External
+tokens belong in `externalContracts.ts`, which is currently empty (`:14`).
+
+**Fix:** move the entry verbatim:
+
+```typescript
+// packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: { address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913", abi: [/* existing USDC abi */] },
+  },
+} as const;
+export default externalContracts satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration;
+```
+
+Then revert `deployedContracts.ts` to its generated state (Payouts only), drop the
+`deployedContracts` import and the `USDC`/`PAYOUTS` consts at `page.tsx:7,10-11`, and
+confirm `yarn next:check-types` still passes.
+
+### 7. Recipient is a raw text input, cast straight to an address
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84`, used at `:55`**
+
+```tsx
+<input type="text" placeholder="0x... recipient address" ... />
+// ...
+args: [recipient as `0x${string}`, ...]
+```
+
+No ENS resolution and no checksum/format validation — the `as` cast just silences
+TypeScript. `vitalik.eth` never resolves, and a truncated or mistyped hex string goes to
+the wallet as-is. For a contract that moves real USDC to an arbitrary recipient this is
+the highest-consequence input on the page.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```tsx
+import { AddressInput } from "@scaffold-ui/components";
+<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="Recipient address or ENS" />
+```
+
+and disable **Send Payout** unless `isAddress(recipient)`.
+
+### 8. Approve and Send Payout are both always live
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`**
+
+The page never reads `allowance`, so both buttons render permanently and there is no
+ordering cue. New users click **Send Payout** first, `transferFrom` reverts on the
+`Payouts: transfer failed` require, and issue 5 means they see nothing at all.
+Experienced users re-approve needlessly and burn an extra tx.
+
+**Fix:** read the allowance and render exactly one action.
+
+```tsx
+const { data: allowance } = useScaffoldReadContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+  functionName: "allowance",
+  args: [connectedAddress, PAYOUTS_ADDRESS],
+});
+const needsApproval = (allowance ?? 0n) < parseUnits(amount || "0", 6);
+```
+
+Render **Approve** when `needsApproval`, **Send Payout** otherwise. Refetch the allowance
+after the approve confirms.
+
+### 9. Event feed queries Base from block 0
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:29-34`**
+
+```tsx
+fromBlock: 0n,
+watch: true,
+```
+
+Base is past 33.7M blocks. This walks the entire chain history on every page load. On a
+public/shared-key endpoint (issue 11) it will be rate-limited or rejected outright, so
+the payouts feed most likely renders "No payouts yet." in production while working fine
+against a local chain. The generated contract entry already records the answer:
+`deployedContracts.ts:47` → `deployedOnBlock: 33712450`.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```tsx
+fromBlock: deployedContracts[8453].Payouts.deployedOnBlock ?? 33712450n,
+```
+
+(as `BigInt(...)`). Verify the feed populates against Base mainnet before shipping.
+
+### 10. Hardcoded dark wrapper breaks light mode
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65`**
+
+```tsx
+<div className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white">
+```
+
+This bypasses DaisyUI entirely. The footer still ships `<SwitchTheme/>`
+(`components/Footer.tsx:43`), so a light-mode user gets a black page with light-theme
+header and footer bolted on, and the theme toggle appears broken. The hand-rolled
+`border-gray-700` on the feed rows (`:121`) has the same problem — invisible in light mode.
+
+**Fix:** `<div className="min-h-screen bg-base-200 text-base-content">` and
+`border-base-300` on the rows. If you genuinely want dark-only, set `data-theme="dark"`
+on `<html>` in `app/layout.tsx` and remove `<SwitchTheme/>` — don't do it per-page.
+
+### 11. Production RPC and WalletConnect run on shared scaffold defaults
+**`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:16,29,32-35,40`**
+
+```typescript
+alchemyApiKey: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY || DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY,
+rpcOverrides: { /* empty */ },
+walletConnectProjectId: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID || '3a8170812b534d0ff9d794f19a901d64',
+```
+
+Both fall back to SE-2's public demo credentials shared across every scaffold project.
+Worse, `services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx:20` deliberately *deprioritises* the Alchemy URL
+when the default key is detected, so Base traffic goes to the bare `http()` public
+endpoint first. `.env.example` ships both vars empty and there is no `.env.local`, so
+unless they are set in the Vercel project this is what real users get: rate-limited
+reads, a feed that doesn't load, and WalletConnect sessions on a demo project id.
+
+**Fix:** set `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` in
+the Vercel production env (not just in the repo), or pin a dedicated Base endpoint:
+
+```typescript
+rpcOverrides: { [chains.base.id]: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL as string },
+```
+
+Then confirm in the deployed app's network tab that requests actually hit your endpoint.
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 12. 30s polling makes an L2 app feel broken
+**`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24`** — `pollingInterval: 30000`
+
+Base blocks are ~2s. After a payout confirms, the balance and feed can sit stale for half
+a minute, which is what drives the double-click in issue 4.
+
+**Fix:** drop to `3000`, and explicitly refetch balance + allowance in the write's
+`onBlockConfirmation` rather than waiting for a poll.
+
+### 13. `loading` class on a `btn` swallows the label
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101,108`**
+
+```tsx
+className={`btn btn-primary ${isPending ? "loading" : ""}`}
+```
+
+DaisyUI replaces the entire button content with a spinner — mid-transaction the user sees
+two unlabelled spinners and cannot tell which action is running.
+
+**Fix:** keep the label, add an inline spinner:
+
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={isMining} onClick={handlePay}>
+  {isMining && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm" />}
+  Send Payout
+</button>
+```
+
+### 14. Hand-rolled `shorten()` instead of `<Address/>`
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:13`, used at `:122,124`**
+
+The feed shows bare truncated hex — no ENS name, no blockie, no copy button, no Basescan
+link. On a payouts feed, "did this go to the right person" is the entire question being
+asked, and truncation is exactly how address-substitution mistakes hide.
+
+**Fix:** `import { Address } from "@scaffold-ui/components";` and render
+`<Address address={payout.args.to} chain={targetNetwork} />`. Delete `shorten`.
+
+### 15. The Payouts contract address is never shown
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:64-76`**
+
+The page shows the user's balance but never says which contract it is asking them to
+approve unlimited-ish spend against. Approving a contract you can't see is the exact
+shape users are told to refuse.
+
+**Fix:** render `<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} chain={targetNetwork} />` near the
+Approve button, labelled "Payouts contract".
+
+### 16. Balance and feed never refresh after a payout
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:23-34`**
+
+Neither `useScaffoldReadContract` result is refetched post-confirmation; the balance is
+left to the 30s poll (issue 12) and `watch: true` on the event history re-runs the
+block-0 scan (issue 9) rather than doing a targeted refresh.
+
+**Fix:** capture `refetch` from the read hooks and call them in the write's
+`onBlockConfirmation`, keeping the button locked until they resolve.
+
+### 17. Loading state renders as a real value
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:75`**
+
+```tsx
+{usdcBalance !== undefined ? formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6) : "0"}
+```
+
+While the read is in flight — and whenever it fails, e.g. after issue 6 wipes the USDC
+entry — the user is told they have **0 USDC**, which reads as a fact, not as "loading".
+
+**Fix:** use the hook's `isLoading` and render
+`<span className="loading loading-spinner loading-xs" />`, and distinguish the error case.
+
+### 18. Amount input accepts values the contract will reject
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:85-91`**
+
+`type="number"` permits negatives, `e`-notation, and more than 6 decimal places.
+`parseUnits("1.2345678", 6)` silently truncates the 7th decimal, and a negative or zero
+amount reverts on `Payouts: zero amount` with no message (issue 5). There is also no
+check against `usdcBalance`.
+
+**Fix:** use SE-2's `IntegerInput`-style guarded input or clamp to 6 decimals and
+`> 0`, and disable **Send Payout** when the amount exceeds the balance.
+
+### 19. Branding is still stock Scaffold-ETH across the board
+- **`packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx:11-12`** — tab title `Scaffold-ETH 2 App`, description
+  `Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2`. This is what shows in the browser tab and in every link
+  preview of the shipped product.
+- **`packages/nextjs/utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:8`** — title template
+  `"%s | Scaffold-ETH 2"`.
+- **`packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx:22,30-45`** — the landing page still says "Welcome to
+  Scaffold-ETH 2" and tells users to edit `page.tsx` and `YourContract.sol`. This is the
+  first screen real users hit; it should introduce the payouts product and link `/payouts`.
+- **`packages/nextjs/components/Footer.tsx:50-74`** — "Fork me" → scaffold-eth/se-2,
+  BuidlGuidl credit, and a Support link pointing at the SE-2 Telegram. Your users will
+  file payout problems in someone else's support channel.
+- **`packages/nextjs/public/manifest.json`** — `Scaffold-ETH 2 DApp`.
+- **`packages/nextjs/public/favicon.png`** and `thumbnail.jpg` — stock scaffold assets.
+- **`README.md:1`** — still the upstream SE-2 readme; nothing about the payouts app,
+  Base deployment, or required env vars.
+
+**Fix:** set real title/description/template, rewrite the landing page and footer links to
+your own repo and support channel, replace favicon/thumbnail/manifest, and rewrite the
+README with the deployed addresses and the `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars from issue 11.
+
+### 20. Pill-shaped inputs clip content
+**`packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36` and `:63`** — `--radius-field: 9999rem;`
+
+Fully-rounded fields against `--radius-box: 0rem` looks unintentional, and the long
+address string in the recipient field (issue 7) runs into the rounded caps.
+
+**Fix:** set `--radius-field: 0.5rem;` in **both** `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks —
+at theme level, not with per-component `rounded-*` overrides.
+
+### 21. Phantom users cannot connect
+**`packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:2-9,20-28`**
+
+The wallet list is MetaMask / WalletConnect / Ledger / Base Account / Rainbow / Safe.
+Phantom has a large EVM user base on Base and is absent, so those users have no working
+entry point at all.
+
+**Fix:** `import { phantomWallet } from "@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/wallets";` and add it to
+the `wallets` array.
+
+### 22. WalletConnect app name is `scaffold-eth-2`
+**`packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:49`**
+
+This string is what the wallet shows in its connection-approval sheet. Users are asked to
+approve a USDC spend for an app calling itself "scaffold-eth-2".
+
+**Fix:** set `appName` to the product name.
+
+### 23. No mobile WalletConnect redirect
+**`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:36-62`**
+
+On a phone connected over WalletConnect, tapping Approve or Send Payout fires the write
+but leaves the user on the browser page — they have to find and switch to the wallet app
+by hand to see the signing request. Combined with issue 5, a mobile user who doesn't know
+to switch apps sees nothing happen at all.
+
+**Fix:** after calling the write (never before — navigating away first means the write
+never fires), deep-link to the connected wallet, targeting the connector the user actually
+used, and skip it when running inside a wallet's in-app browser. Test on a real phone.
+
+### 24. Confirm the deployed contract is verified on Basescan
+**`packages/hardhat/deploy/00_deploy_payouts.ts`** — no `packages/hardhat/deployments/`
+directory is checked in, so verification status can't be confirmed from the repo.
+
+An unverified contract that users are asked to grant USDC allowance to reads as something
+to hide, and nobody can inspect `pay` before approving.
+
+**Fix:** run `yarn verify --network base` and confirm the source shows on Basescan. Commit
+the `deployments/` artifacts so the deployed address and block are reproducible.

